From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:10:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] make the docked lid policy configurable, lock and
 action separately

The previous fix hoisted a single ignoreLidCloseWhenDocked flag to cover
the whole lid-close response, which cured the bug -- a docked machine no
longer locked when it should stay usable -- but coupled two decisions that
tdepowersave keeps separate everywhere else, and left the flag with no UI.

Replace it with two settings in [General], each defaulting off:

  lockOnLidCloseWhenDocked   lock the screen on lid close while docked
  performLidActionWhenDocked run the configured lid-close action while docked

Both off is the previous default -- an external display connected means
the session stays usable with the lid shut, neither locking nor acting --
so behaviour is unchanged until the operator asks otherwise. Setting them
independently expresses the cases the single flag could not: docked and
still lock for security, or docked and still suspend, without forcing both
or neither.

Docked stays defined as externalDisplayConnected(): a state of the machine,
not a preference, so it is detected rather than configured. The model is
deliberately two plain toggles rather than a mirror of logind's
docked/external-power/normal policy triplet: tdepowersave runs on systems
with no logind, and coupling the design to a systemd interface would not
travel.

Both toggles are exposed in the configure dialog beside "Lock screen on
lid close", hidden together with it on non-laptops, and the docked lock
counts toward enabling the lock-method combo. Loaded, saved and wired to
general_valueChanged() like the controls around them.

Signed-off-by: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
